<title>USA: Digital Q3 revs, margin fall from year ago.</title>
<headline>Digital Q3 revs, margin fall from year ago.</headline>
<dateline>MAYNARD, Mass. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Digital Equipment Corp said Thursday its total operating revenues for the fiscal third quarter fell to $3.31 billion from $3.62 billion a year earlier.</p>
<p>Gross margin fell to 33.4 percent from 34.6 percent a year ago but was up from 32.9 percent in the fiscal second quarter.</p>
<p>DEC reported third quarter net income of $51 million, or $0.27 a share, down from $124 million, or $0.74 a share, a year ago. The First Call consensus estimate for the quarter, ended March 29, was $0.24 a share.</p>
</text>
